holes_default_param: coverage audit: test/refine_audit/holes/default_param.march:9:27: param `f` #1: b > 0: this refinement was declared here, but no occurrence with the same enclosing name and predicate text survives desugaring: either the declared type was discarded entirely (a multi-head function's clause merge drops every parameter type before the checker ever sees it) or it now lives only under a mangled name a plain call cannot resolve to (a default-argument function's arity variant, e.g. `f$2`). See specs/todos/2026-09-03-desugar-dropped-refinement-unchecked.md.
